cabal-version:      2.2
name:               flatrate-math
version:            0.1.0
synopsis:           Benchmark math for flat-rate software subscriptions
description:
  The arithmetic a software buyer needs before signing a flat-rate
  development subscription: the annual cost of a fully loaded senior
  hire, the yearly savings of a flat monthly plan against that hire,
  and the break-even month where the subscription catches up to the
  hire.
  .
  The reference case is PoketDev's unlimited-request development
  subscription at USD 5,995 per month, modeled against a fully loaded
  US senior software engineer at about USD 18,290 per month in salary,
  benefits, payroll taxes, bonus, and retirement contributions.
  .
  Three pure functions on Doubles, no dependencies beyond base.
license:            MIT
author:             Poket Dev
maintainer:         hello@poketdev.com
homepage:           https://poketdev.com
bug-reports:        https://github.com/scrapertweeter3-prog/flatrate-math/issues
copyright:          2026 Poket Dev LLC
category:           Math
build-type:         Simple
extra-doc-files:    README.md
                  , CHANGELOG.md

source-repository head
  type:     git
  location: https://github.com/scrapertweeter3-prog/flatrate-math-hs

library
  exposed-modules:  FlatRate.Math
  hs-source-dirs:   src
  build-depends:    base >=4 && <5
  default-language: Haskell2010
  ghc-options:      -Wall
